## 3  Result and Discussion
## 3.1  Characterization
MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe was obtained on the basis of previously reported method with a rods-like shape. From the SEM image in Fig. 1, our-prepared MIL-88 $\left(\mathrm{NH}_{2}\right)$ -Fe $@$ CNTs still maintain the original morphology, evenly distributed, with the introduction of acidized CNTs. Crystalline structures of as-prepared samples were characterized by XRD. Several peaks of MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe are agree with the reported works [34–37]. The similar diffraction peaks between MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe and MIL- ${\cdot}88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe $@$ CNTs in Fig. 2a reveals that the crystal structure of the prepared nanocomposites have no obvious change. To explore the effect of modification on the chemical structure especially the functional groups, FT-IR was performed. The peaks located at $769~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ and $1258~\mathrm{cm^{-1}}$ were clearly observed on two samples, which should attribute to C-H bending vibration of benzene ring and $\mathrm{C-N}$ respectively. And the peaks corresponding to the asymmetric stretching of the carboxyl groups were also identified at $1383~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ and $1575~\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ . Note that the peaks of CNTs are invisible [38], maybe due to the small content of SWNTs. In MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe $@$ CNTs, the peaks show slight movements, indicating the effective hydrogen bonds and $\pi{-}\pi$ interactions between MIL$88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe and CNTs [31]. In this regard, the structure of CNT-modified MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe remains unchanged. The difference between MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe and MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ - Fe@CNTs can been seen through TEM. As depicted in TEM image (Fig. 3), it was found that some tubular architecture (CNTs) interweave with the MIL-88 $\mathrm{(NH}_{2})$ -Fe of rods-like shape. The above results reveal the successful synthesis of MIL-88 $\left(\mathrm{NH}_{2}\right)$ -Fe $@$ CNTs.
3.2  Effect of CNTs on the Peroxidase‑like Activity of MIL‑88 $(\mathsf{N H}_{2})$ ‑Fe with or without DNA
It was found that the peroxidase-like activity of MOFs could be promoted or inhibited by DNA through influencing the interaction between the enzyme mimics and substrates [39–42]. Hence, based on the typical TMB- ${\bf\cdot H}_{2}{\bf O}_{2}$ catalytic chromogenic reaction, the effect of CNTs on the catalytic activity of MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe with or without DNA was explored. As shown in Fig. 4, the peroxidase-like activities of as-prepared samples were determined with TMB as the substrates in the presence of ${\bf H}_{2}{\bf O}_{2}$ . The typical absorption band of oxidation state of TMB (oxTMB) at $652~\mathrm{nm}$ was clearly observed in the system containing catalysts. Interestingly, the peroxidase-like activity of CNT-modified $\mathrm{MIL}{-}88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe was superior to that of MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe alone in the absence of DNA (curves c and d). Here, the Tauc plots were fitted in Fig. 5. The band gaps of MIL$88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe and MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe@CNTs were tested to be $1.25\ \mathrm{eV}$ and $0.33\ \mathrm{eV}$ . The narrower band gap promotes a faster electron transfer process, and thus helps the enhancement of catalytic activity. In other words, the modification of CNTs can effectively improve the catalytic activity of $\mathrm{{MIL}}{\cdot}88(\mathrm{{NH}}_{2})–$ Fe, which is consistent with reported works [31]. Therefore, based on the higher peroxidase-like activity of our-prepared nanocomposites, the ultrasensitive detection of ${\mathrm{H}}_{2}{\mathrm{O}}_{2}$ as an example was achieved. As shown in Fig. 6a, the absorbance intensity at $652\mathrm{nm}$ (typical absorption peak of oxTMB) increased with the increasing concentration of $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ . And the detection limit (LOD) of ${\bf H}_{2}{\bf O}_{2}$ was calculated to $17.64\upmu\mathrm{g/L}(3\upsigma/\mathrm{k}).$ representing the highly sensitive performance of the MIL-88( $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe $@$ CNTs-based colorimetric sensors.
Furthermore, it was confirmed that the CNT-modified nanocomposites further enhance the oxidation degree towards TMB substrates while the adsorption of DNA has brought the higher peroxidase-like catalytic activity (curves a and b in Fig. 4). Accordingly, it can be inferred that the desirable affinity of CNTs to DNA via ${\pi}-{\pi}$ stacking strengthen the adsorption of DNA on the MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe, which contributes to the TMB substrates binding and catalytic activity enhancement.
## 3.3  Possible Mechanism Analysis
As mentioned above, DNA adsorption is an important factor affecting catalytic activity. In the following experiments, ssDNA (single-stranded DNA) was adopt unless otherwise stated. First, the effect of different sequence of DNA on activity enhancement was explored. As shown in Fig. 7a, poly-C22 and poly-G22 effectively promoted the catalytic oxidation of TMB substrates. However, similar to condition of without DNA, both poly-A22 and poly-T22 have no effect on the catalytic activity, which may be contributed to the acidic environment in this reaction system. According to the $\mathsf{p K}_{\mathrm{a}}$ values, protonation of guanine and cytosine enabled the surface charges change, thus strengthening the interaction between the catalysts and DNA and the catalytic oxidation of TMB. G22 has regulation on both of MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe and MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{\cdot}$ )-Fe $@$ CNTs, while MIL- $88\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ )-Fe $@$ CNTs with G22 has a better regulation (Figure S2). Moreover, the improved catalytic activity was also related to the length of DNA. One can see that the oxidation degree of TMB gradually enhances with the increasing DNA length in Fig. 7b, showing that the poly-G30 with more binding sites exhibited the strongest effect on the catalytic activity. In addition, the absorbance intensity of oxTMB did no longer increase when the concentration of DNA beyond $5~{\upmu\mathrm{M}}$ (Fig. 7c), which may be caused by the saturation of DNA on the surface of MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe@CNTs.
Considering that $\mathsf{p H}$ value may play an important role in the catalytic reaction, the oxidation of TMB under different $\mathrm{\pH}$ ranging from 4 to 8 was determined. From the Fig. 7d, it can be concluded that the adsorption of DNA on the prepared MIL- $88(\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe $@$ CNTs depends on pH values. As the $\mathrm{\pH}$ value increased, the absorbance intensity distinctly decreased and the optimal $\mathrm{\pH}$ were set as 4. The surface charges on the prepared nanocomposites would be altered with the $\mathrm{\pH}$ -induced protonation of the carboxyl groups contained in the prepared nanocomposites.
## 4  Conclusions
In summary, we fabricated the MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2}\mathrm{,}$ -Fe $@$ CNTs with controlled catalytic activity by ssDNA. Compared with pure MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe nanorods, the introduction of CNTs enables the nanocomposites’ better affinity to DNA and enhancement of peroxidase-like activity, which achieves flexible regulation of their catalytic activity. It was because that the negatively charged ssDNA altered the surface charge properties of the nanocomposites to increase the electrostatic interaction between catalyst and substrates. Beyond that, the significant enhancement of the adsorption capacity towards ssDNA in the presence of CNTs was verified. We explore the switchable catalytic activity regulated by different length or sequence of ssDNA. Besides, the narrower bandgap of MIL-88 $\mathrm{NH}_{2})$ -Fe $@$ CNTs is indeed conductive to accelerate electron transfer process, thus have a positive effect on the catalytic oxidation of substrates. Our study revealed that as-prepared nanocomposites with adsorbed ssDNA showed excellent affinity to substrates and high catalytic reaction rate according to Michaelis–Menten kinetics. More importantly, with the aid of good affinity of CNTs to DNA, our-prepared MIL-88 $\left(\mathrm{NH}_{2}\right)$ -Fe $@$ CNTs exhibit enhanced DNA adsorption capacity, which pave the way of achieving ultrasensitive assays of various pollutants in actual environment.
